        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:46:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63510,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrium</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:46:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63511,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>It is most commonly diagnosed in perimenopause, with symptoms of abnormal, non-cyclical vaginal bleeding. The endometrium shows increased thickness on ultrasound.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-07T15:19:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63512,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Risk factors include perimenopause, obesity, polycystic ovarian syndrome, and diabetes {18682485}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:46:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63513,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Prolonged exposure to unopposed estrogen is a risk factor.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:46:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63514,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperplasia without atypia is the result of prolonged estrogen exposure unopposed by progesterone or progestational agents acting on the entire endometrial field {22290745}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:46:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63515,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "<p>The endometrium varies from having the uniform, tan appearance of the late proliferative phase to appearing highly thickened and sometimes polypoid or spongy with cysts.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-07T15:19:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63516,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tubular glands are admixed with branching and/or cystically dilated glands, often irregularly distributed, creating increased gland density with variable ratios of glands to stroma. The epithelium is simple, but staggered nuclei can confer a pseudostratified appearance. Higher estrogen levels drive mitoses and round up nuclei, whereas waning levels produce mitotically quiescent round or elongated nuclei. Key to the diagnosis is the uniform distribution in all submitted tissue, sometimes punctuated by randomly scattered tubal metaplasia, fibrin thrombi, and stromal breakdown.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:46:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63517,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:46:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63518,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:46:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63519,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em>&nbsp;increased endometrial gland&ndash;to&ndash;stroma ratio; tubular, branching, and/or cystically dilated glands resembling proliferative endometrium; uniform distribution of nuclear features across submitted tissue.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-24T16:12:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63520,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T16:46:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63521,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 220,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "<p>Women exposed to unopposed estrogen have a 3&ndash;4-fold increased risk of endometrial carcinoma, rising to 10-fold after a decade {4005805}. Progression to well-differentiated endometrial carcinoma occurs in 1&ndash;3% of women with hyperplasia without atypia.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-24T16:13:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]